---
description: DART hybrid parser engineering rules (normalize -> anchor rule engine -> SLM fallback)
alwaysApply: true
---

- Follow `AGENTS.md` at the repository root; it is the source of truth for principles and conventions.
- Never parse HTML styles. Flatten `colspan`/`rowspan` into a 2D grid before any table logic.
- Prefer Open DART XBRL for financial statements; HTML parsing is the fallback.
- Rule engine first; invoke the SLM fallback only when validation fails. Both outputs must conform to `src/dart_parser/fallback/schemas.py`.
- All numeric cell conversions go through `to_number()`; all text comparisons go through `normalize_text()`.
- Keep the three states apart: `missing` (failure), `not_applicable`, `not_in_regime`.
- Add or update a pytest alongside every parser change, using mock HTML snippets.
- Extraction item definitions live in `docs/standard-extraction-items.md`; do not invent new item keys without updating that document.
